# MIDI in's pads (0.15.8, the MIDI IN settings page after SET): Notes PADS makes a pad controller (an MPC's default pad map: bank A from note 36)
# play PERF. Bank A: the drums on pads 1-6, the performance on 7-16 (9 breakdown ...); banks B-D the pluck, bass, acid in key; bank E the chords.
# Channel: all, or one. SCALE (the default) keeps channel 1 notes editing the scale, as before.
seed 0
wait 3000
press HOME
wait 900
release HOME
wait 100
expect fxpage 18
turn SELECT 5
wait 100
expect fxpage 26
expect minpads 0
expect minch 0
spin K1 1
wait 200
expect minpads 1
midi 90 24 64
wait 100
shot midi_in_page.png
tap FX
wait 200
# the seeded piece is A natural minor: bank E pad 6 (note 105) is VI, F
midi 90 69 64
wait 300
expect chordroot 5
midi 80 69 00
# bank E pad 1 (note 100): home, A
midi 90 64 64
wait 300
expect chordroot 9
# bank A pad 1 (note 36): the kick, at once
midi 99 24 7F
wait 20
expect drumglow0 1
midi 89 24 00
# bank B pad 1 (note 52): the pluck on the root (A3 = 57), and its note off
midi 90 34 64
wait 50
expect padnote0 57
midi 80 34 00
wait 50
expect padnote0 0
# bank C pad 3 (note 70): the bass on the scale's third tone (C4 = 60, played two octaves up the key: 84)
midi 90 46 64
wait 50
expect padnote18 84
midi 90 46 00
wait 50
expect padnote18 0
# bank A pad 9 (note 44): the breakdown, on the bar
midi 90 2C 64
wait 2500
expect sec 1
# bank A pad 7 (note 42): all the drums muted, in the engine too (0.16.12: it only showed), then back
midi 90 2A 64
wait 200
expect trkmute 15
expect entrkmute 15
midi 90 2A 64
wait 200
expect entrkmute 0
# the channel: 2 only, so a pad on channel 1 does nothing
press HOME
wait 900
release HOME
wait 100
turn SELECT 5
wait 100
expect fxpage 26
spin K2 2
wait 200
expect minch 2
tap FX
wait 200
midi 90 69 64
wait 300
expect chordroot 9
midi 91 69 64
wait 300
expect chordroot 5
# kept with the settings
tap PLAY
wait 5000
reboot
wait 3000
expect minpads 1
expect minch 2
